WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.840
- She's the original
flag girl and has been

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.787
holding it down ever
since her debut album,

00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:05.150
"All Hail the Queen."

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.050
She went on to win Grammys,
Emmys, Golden Globes

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.630
and she was nominated for an Oscar

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.830
for her role as Mama in "Chicago."

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.891
Give it up for Queen Latifah, y'all.

00:00:13.891 --> 00:00:17.724
(audience applauds)

00:00:17.724 --> 00:00:20.510
Yes! Bravo, bravo.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.670
We need to get you an EGOT at this point.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.220
You're missing one.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.790
- Gonna get my EGOT on.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.360
- Yeah. I mean, EGT is still great.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.254
So I'm not frowning at that.

00:00:30.254 --> 00:00:33.680
So, did you hear the twins'
reaction to your song?

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:34.840
What did you think?

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.908
- That's so cute, oh my goodness.

00:00:37.908 --> 00:00:40.009
Aw, man, that's cool.

00:00:40.009 --> 00:00:40.867
I think that's cool.

00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:41.990
I think that's cool.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:42.823
- Isn't it funny?

00:00:42.823 --> 00:00:44.510
Like a whole different
generation, like, gets to hear...

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.010
I just love them listening to songs

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.620
that I've, like, used to rollerskate to,

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.800
or like grew up with, and,
like, it's their first time.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.890
It's crazy. If you watch all
their series, it's hilarious.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.010
Cause it's these songs you'd
think that they'd know.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.940
And then they're, like, so shocked by it.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.030
It's awesome.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.090
So wait, I actually heard
something interesting.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.580
You're a country music fan, which I love.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.837
So what song is like,
one of your favorites?

00:01:05.837 --> 00:01:07.620
- "Devil Went Down to Georgia."

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.069
- What? I love that.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.840
- Really, that was kind of a rap record,

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:12.870
if you think about it.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:17.870
Like, it was like... that was
like a country rap record.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.900
I was like, wait a minute.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.069
You know, this is dope.

00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:24.100
I heard something from Florida,
Georgia line the other day.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.820
I don't know the name of the song,

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:29.365
but I was like, the pocket of
the song felt very hip hop.

00:01:29.365 --> 00:01:30.198
- Yeah.

00:01:30.198 --> 00:01:31.970
- But the song was very country.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:33.636
- Yeah.
- You know what I mean?

00:01:33.636 --> 00:01:36.940
So I was like, I liked their
combination of it, you know?

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.960
And I love that country
music is now, like,

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:43.352
really think country music is

00:01:43.352 --> 00:01:47.030
really leaning into so
many other genres now.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.730
I think it's pulling
from a little hip hop.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.080
It's pulling from a little R&amp;B, maybe.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.630
It's always, like, got,
like, blues under it, too.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:56.494
- Yeah.
- So like, but I think it...

00:01:56.494 --> 00:01:58.880
I like it pulling from
some of, like, the hip hop,

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.577
the track kind of, you
know, pockets, you know.

00:02:01.577 --> 00:02:04.220
You starting to hear
some of that in the songs

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.520
that you didn't really hear before.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.950
And I actually was going to go
to the Country Music Awards,

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:13.780
the last one, because I really
just, I love some of those.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:16.160
I just love some of those performances.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.563
And they're funny to me.

00:02:17.563 --> 00:02:19.877
You know, like, I like watching usually

00:02:19.877 --> 00:02:20.893
when Blake and Luke just
like snap on each other

00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:26.700
for an hour or two, just
crack jokes on each other.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.720
I'm like, that's funny, too.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.400
But I think, yeah, I like Carrie Underwood

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.940
and anything you do is
just like, come on girl.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.270
- Oh, you're so nice.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:38.740
You don't need to
compliment me ever again.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:39.690
You've made my life.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.600
So, I love that you know me.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.360
All right, so I saw you're
starring in a TV reboot

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.330
of "The Equalizer,"
which I love those films.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:47.310
So how is that going?

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.583
- It's going.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.880
You know, we were two
days away from shooting

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.480
and then the world shut down.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:54.313
- Yeah.

00:02:54.313 --> 00:02:56.530
- And now we are about to be shooting

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.530
in less than eight weeks, you know?

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.460
So, it just like turned
back on real quick.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:02.773
So now I'm like, oh!

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.530
It's exciting because the
TV show I used to watch

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:13.280
when I was a kid, and then of course

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.470
we fell in love with the Denzel movies,

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:18.380
but now I get to create
my own version of it.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.780
And I'm a woman as well.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.130
So I'm a woman who gets
to kick some behind.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.020
- Yes!

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:26.260
- But, you know, "The
Equalizer" is about justice.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.940
It's about making things equal.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.590
It's about fighting for, you know, people

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:32.476
who can't fight for themselves

00:03:32.476 --> 00:03:35.820
with this amazing skill set, you know?

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:39.060
So, I get to like, you know,

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.360
I get to mete some justice out there,

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.500
and I'm looking forward to it.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.010
I get to use the hands.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:47.373
I'm like da da da da, you
know, get to do some shooting,

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.260
do some driving.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.420
I'm going to go on my motorcycle, so -

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.840
- Oh my gosh, you're living
my, like, dream life.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.240
This is awesome.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.250
And a fact that the woman...
a fact that a woman's doing...

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.950
'cause I love the Denzel movies.

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.340
I mean, I've seen them so much,

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.720
I literally, I could recite the script.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.120
So, but I love that a woman's doing it.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.950
And I think that it's just a
completely different respect

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.234
of what a cool way to
like reboot it for TV.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:13.350
And like you said, just a
woman, like bringing justice.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.183
Like, I just...

00:04:14.183 --> 00:04:16.620
ain't no woman like a
woman pissed off, y'all.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.633
Like, so I'm so excited.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.570
Hey, before we go, though,
I want you to tell me,

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:24.820
you've got a huge event tomorrow.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:25.750
So, what's going on?

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:28.130
- Huge event tomorrow.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:32.570
Doing the hashtag
#Act4Impact livestream event,

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:34.640
Saturday, September 26th.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.150
It will be at 7:00 PM eastern time.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.590
It's with the American Lung Association.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:42.450
It's a live stream event to raise money

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:46.764
for people who have been
impacted by COVID-19,

00:04:46.764 --> 00:04:50.710
particularly black and brown communities,

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:54.930
those underserved communities
who've been really hit hard.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.703
They're going to advocate for us.

00:04:56.703 --> 00:04:59.455
They recognized that this
was going to be a problem

00:04:59.455 --> 00:05:00.780
way back in April,

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.250
so they started the
COVID-19 Action Initiative

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.699
to raise money, to protect people.

00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:11.260
They want to give out masks, you know,

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.920
so people can protect themselves.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.900
Those who don't have
them or can't get them.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:19.632
They want to prevent
it, you know, obviously,

00:05:19.632 --> 00:05:23.130
and they want to make
sure they can do research,

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.080
make sure that when the vaccines are ready

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.110
that they go to those who
really need them, you know?

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.810
There are people that have been out there

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:31.700
on the front lines.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:34.030
And so, the black and brown communities,

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:36.753
we've been getting hit particularly hard

00:05:36.753 --> 00:05:39.010
and pretty much

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:42.328
because of financial
issues as well, you know.

00:05:42.328 --> 00:05:43.161
- Yeah.

00:05:43.161 --> 00:05:45.010
- And this whole thing has
brought, like, a huge light

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:48.880
to the disparities
between black and white.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.220
Well, not just black and white,

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.300
but white people and everybody else,

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.200
you know, when it comes
to the healthcare system.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.500
So, I think this is...

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.410
So many people, especially
a lot of my white friends,

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.590
and I'm sure yours and everybody,

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.290
has been like, what can
we do, what can we do?

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.440
Well, here's one of the things you can do.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.530
Help people out.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:13.130
You know, help people who really need it.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:16.160
And this event that we're having

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.330
is going to be a lot of fun.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:19.870
We're going to have, you
know, some of my friends

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.740
like Jimmy Fallon, Jill Scott.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:26.740
We got Common, Questlove,
Gagle, Dwayne, Keke Palmer.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:28.640
We got performances.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:31.010
Fitz and the Tantrums are
going to come perform,

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.560
but people are going to perform

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.630
and tell their stories

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.860
about how it's affected their families.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:39.450
And we're also going to
have real doctors on there

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:43.670
to explain and educate so that people

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:46.260
really understand what's happening.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:50.570
Take the politics out of it
and really just understand it

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:54.660
so that we can all come
together and fight this thing.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:56.650
- Yeah, I know. Agreed, agreed.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.210
I can not wait to watch it.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:06:59.640
That's amazing.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.270
And I can't... I'm one of those kids

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.103
that loves to learn as well.

00:07:02.103 --> 00:07:04.550
So I can't wait to hear
all the doctors as well.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:07.760
Well, okay. So, speaking
of having a good time,

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.760
I love food.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.100
So, there's no segue for this.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:15.500
So, I'm bringing this up because
I think this is hilarious.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:19.350
Did you know that someone
honored you with a sandwich?

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:20.650
Did you know that there's a sandwich

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.573
named after you and it's awesome?

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:24.263
- What?

00:07:24.263 --> 00:07:26.030
- Yes. And I'm so jealous.

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:27.810
I want a sandwich.

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:30.640
So, Sammich Restaurant in Ashland, Oregon

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.073
is serving the Queen LaBEEFa.

00:07:34.226 --> 00:07:36.643
(they laugh)

00:07:38.118 --> 00:07:40.451
The Queen LaBEEFa, come on.

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:45.230
- My assistant, Jonathan, is handing me -

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:47.230
- A Queen LaBEEFa, yes!

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.270
Okay, y'all it come?

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:49.620
I love you so much, Justin.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.390
It comes with steak,
jalapeno cream cheese spread

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.180
and red onion on sourdough rye.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.720
So, I'm just saying we should taste it.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:58.370
It's a Queen LaBEEFa.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.953
Cause it's just never... that's
never going to not be funny.

00:08:00.953 --> 00:08:04.343
This is the largest sandwich
in the entire world.

00:08:06.055 --> 00:08:06.888
- My god.

00:08:06.888 --> 00:08:08.420
- Oh, damn. That's good.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.253
Yeah.

00:08:09.253 --> 00:08:10.086
- Is it good?

00:08:10.086 --> 00:08:11.830
- Yes. It's so good.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:13.780
Your Queen LaBEEFa sandwich is so good.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:18.580
- Look, I'm about to spray
my Queen LaBEEFa sandwich.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:21.552
- COVID friendly.

00:08:21.552 --> 00:08:23.330
It is so good.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.110
You've got to try it. It's so good.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:27.330
Thank you so much, Sammich
Restaurant in Ashland, Oregon.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:29.300
That was amazing.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.660
All right, so be sure, y'all..

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:32.060
See, you like it, don't you?

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:33.510
It's so good. Get that little bit.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:34.559
Yup.

00:08:34.559 --> 00:08:37.392
(audience laughs)

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.070
You're so classy.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:41.900
I totally talked with my mouth open.

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:44.270
I got to take lessons
on class from the Queen.

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:45.740
- It's all about this right here.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:47.230
- That's me, too!

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:50.360
Yes, it's so good.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:51.316
Yeah. I'm into that, too.

00:08:51.316 --> 00:08:52.774
- Has that little kick, a little kick.

00:08:52.774 --> 00:08:54.680
- I know, I like some
spice. I like some spice.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.270
Hey, well, thank you
so much for joining us.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.370
Everybody be sure to
watch Queen Latifah host

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:00.450
the #Act4Impact virtual fundraiser

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.590
for the American Lung
Association tomorrow night.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:03.460
It's really important.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.800
It'll be fun, too.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:08.553
You can see it online
at facebook.com/lungusa.

